 "reflection": {
  "text": "The call was correct because three independent lines converged: extreme tubulin texture and intensity increases, microscopist description of bundled microtubules, and unanimous 4/4 NSC atlas votes for Microtubule stabilizers. The strongest discriminators were tub_glcm_contrast z +104 to +115 with tub_std z +32 to +39 and tub_mean z +25 to +30 across doses 5-7, which reads as more and coarser polymer rather than microtubule loss.\n\nSampling high dose first then mid-dose and a mid-dose replicate was efficient: it showed dose-persistence and reproducibility despite the replicate w_1c56739be6 having lower similarity (0.647) and a nucleus-dominated profile. The persistent 4/10 k-neighbour votes for destabilizers were a useful warning that intensity/texture alone partially overlaps stabilizer and destabilizer neighbours.\n\nUnblinding as docetaxel with ChEMBL Tubulin stabiliser agrees with the phenotype-first call and required no revision of the protocol conclusion.",
  "what_was_right": [
   "Interpreted very high tub_glcm_contrast (+108 to +115) plus high tub_std and tub_mean as bundled stabilized polymer, not depolymerization",
   "Used describe_phenotype density-lower with bundled morphology to favor Microtubule stabilizers at 0.85 then 0.93 over destabilizers, Aurora and Eg5",
   "Used compare_to_reference_atlas NSC 2/2 then 4/4 vote to lock the call despite kNN split 6/10 vs 4/10"
  ],
  "what_was_wrong": [
   "Underestimated the stabilizer vs destabilizer neighbour overlap: 4/10 k-neighbours were Microtubule destabilizers in both atlas comparisons, so texture similarity alone was less specific than the NSC vote",
   "Replicate w_1c56739be6 (dose 5 rep 2) shifted to nuclear shape features nuc_solidity z=-33.4 and frac_large_nucleus z=+21.3 with lower stabilizer similarity 0.647, which could have supported Aurora/Eg5 mitotic arrest if atlas voting had not been unanimous"
  ],
  "citations": [
   {
